      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T15:48:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not particularly necessary, but I think we could avoid the need to kill process groups (and the necessity of having special per-platform code that comes from that), but building the binaries in a separate step (i.e. in fetchModule), and then executing them directly.\n\nThis would also mean that the initial invocation of spawnServerProcess does not have a large latency cost, which may mean we can reduce the large timeout window waitForServer has?",
      "revId": "38dc020fd384c005e262e575bee3a9ce06a384f4",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "694bc887_329dc93a",
        "filename": "acme/pebble_notlinux_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 3961206
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T12:43:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is panic the right thing here or should we update the signature to take `t *testing.T` and call `t.Skip(\"pebble testing only supported on Linux\")`? I\u0027m assuming there are conventions I\u0027m unaware of\n\n```suggestion\nfunc spawnServerProcess(t *testing.T, _ string, _ string, _ ...string) {\n\tt.Skip(\"pebble testing only supported on Linux\")\n```\n\nThis is in case it isn\u0027t clear what I was suggesting, not a requirement.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "38dc020fd384c005e262e575bee3a9ce06a384f4",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
